course: dictionary
lesson: 11141
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word «wig» can mean a covering of hair, a judge's uniform, or a slang phrase. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning you need.
explain: «When they bow, their curly wigs get tangled, and Alice has to run off to hide her laughter.» Curly and tangled tell you a wig is a covering of hair worn on the head, like one you might wear in a costume.
explain: «British judges have worn wigs and robes for hundreds of years as a tradition.» Words like court, robes and tradition tell you this wig is part of a uniform, not a joke or a costume.
explain: Slang is different again. «Wig out» means to become very upset or panic. When you meet a slang phrase, check the sentence and swap in your meaning. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and «wig» is one of them.
fact: A «wig» is a covering of real or false hair worn on the head.
fact: People wear wigs to hide baldness, for a costume, or to change how they look.
fact: In some courts, for example in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, judges and barristers wear wigs as part of their uniform.
fact: «Wig out» is slang meaning to become very upset or panic.
exercise: «When they bow, their curly wigs get tangled.» What is a wig in this sentence? | *A covering of real or false hair worn on the head | A judge's robe worn in court | A kind of hairbrush | A paper hat for a party
exercise: Nadia says, «Dad will wig out if we are late.» What does wig out mean? | To buy a new hairstyle | *To become very upset or panic | To dance with joy | To fall asleep quickly
exercise: «British judges have worn wigs and robes for hundreds of years as a tradition.» Why do judges wear wigs? | To keep their heads warm outside | To hide that they are bald | *As part of an old tradition and uniform in court | For a funny costume at a party
test: Mum says, «She really flipped her wig when the dog ate the cake.» What does flipped her wig mean? | Laughed out loud at the dog | *Went crazy and was very upset | Put on a costume | Took off her hairpiece
test: Someone who has lost their hair through illness might wear a wig. Why? | To hear sounds more clearly | To win a race at school | To make their hair grow faster | *To cover their head and feel more comfortable
exam: In «the King wears his crown on top of his wig and looks very uncomfortable», which meaning of wig is used? | A kind of hat made from paper | A judge's uniform in court | To become very upset | *A covering of hair worn on the head
